# Architecture Rules

**Status (2026-09-21):** the swarm_v2 → single-PydanticAI-agent-loop
migration is complete — the old LangGraph coordinator/domain/specialist
pipeline has been deleted from `src/`. See `docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`
for the current system.

1. Cube is the only authority for business metrics — no local heuristic layer resolves a metric/dimension; always validate against the live catalogue (`docs/BUG_SHEET.md` #8).
2. Only the central `SelericAgent` decides the next tool call — no sub-agent or tool decides independently. There is no handoff, no `mission_lead`/`active_specialist` state to persist.
3. Tools never call other tools. Only `Agent → Tool → Agent`.
4. Analytics/causal/prediction tools calculate; they don't independently fetch data — they consume evidence already fetched via the semantic toolset.
5. Every agent loop is bounded (`max_tool_calls`, `max_cube_queries`, etc.) and the bound is actually enforced.
6. Write/action operations always follow propose → validate → preview → confirm → commit → audit — implemented via `conversations/phase7.py`'s `ApprovalRequest`/`RollbackRecord`; new capabilities wire into that, they don't build a parallel flow.
7. A new autonomous agent is added only if there's a genuine isolation boundary that can't be represented as a tool — default assumption is "this is a tool."

Full rationale and the rest of the non-negotiable list: see Claude memory
`feedback_ai_multiagent_principles.md` and `docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`.
